{"root":"pli/ms","translators":["sujato"],"title":"The Chief: a past life story","html":"<article id='ja8'><header><ul><li class='division'><span class='root'>Jātaka </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Stories of Past Lives 8 </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Ekakanipāta </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The Book of the Ones </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Apaṇṇakavagga </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Sure Bet </span></li></ul>\n<h1 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>8. Gāmaṇijātaka </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The Chief: a past life story </span></h1></header>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>“Api ataramānānaṁ, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Even though they do not hurry, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>phalāsāva samijjhati; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>one who hopes for the fruit succeeds. </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Vipakkabrahmacariyosmi, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>I am one whose spiritual life has ripened: </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>evaṁ jānāhi gāmaṇī”ti. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>know this, chief. </span></span></p></blockquote>\n<p class='endsutta'><span class='root'>Gāmaṇijātakaṁ aṭṭhamaṁ. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></p></article>"}
